  <h2 id="disproof">What would make this archive abandon him</h2>
  <p>
    Written down <strong>before</strong> the documents arrive, and published, so that it cannot be
    quietly revised afterwards. Any one of these would do it.
  </p>
  <div class="scroll bleed"><table>
    <tbody>{disproof.map(([h, b]) => (
      <tr><td style="width:26rem"><strong>{h}</strong></td><td class="small">{b}</td></tr>
    ))}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="panel">
    <h3>Why a page says this at all</h3>
    <p>
      An archive that only ever publishes the evidence <em>for</em> its conclusion is not an archive,
      it is a case. This one has had to withdraw four published claims in a week &mdash; a
      transcription taken for a document, a gazette snippet taken for a record, an estate notice
      belonging to another man entirely, and an age read as a contradiction when it was a pattern.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Every one of those was found by opening the source rather than trusting the summary.</strong>
      The list above is the same discipline pointed forward instead of backward.
    </p>
  </div>

